NavigatorLore = {
 {'sees-all-colors','Sees-All-Colors is an Argonian guildmaster of the Fighters Guild, a martial organization working across political borders. Its struggle against Daedric threats offers adventurers a cause beyond the Three Banners War.'},
 {'razum-dar','Razum-dar is a Khajiit operative in the Eyes of the Queen, serving Queen Ayrenn. His work concerns the security of the Aldmeri Dominion, often through intelligence rather than open warfare.'},
 {'abnur tharn','Abnur Tharn is an Imperial battlemage and veteran statesman. His political experience connects him to the troubled Empire and the struggle over its future.'},
 {'vanus galerion','Vanus Galerion founded the Mages Guild to make magical study more widely available. His work represents a tradition of organized scholarship rather than magic reserved for a privileged few.'},
 {'naryu','Naryu Virian is a Dunmer assassin associated with the Morag Tong, a historically sanctioned institution of assassination in Morrowind. Its traditions differ from those of the Dark Brotherhood.'},
 {'queen ayrenn','Ayrenn leads the Aldmeri Dominion, an alliance of Altmer, Bosmer and Khajiit. Her political vision faces resistance from those who oppose cooperation or her rule.'},
 {'worm cult','The Worm Cult is a necromantic organization associated with Mannimarco and Molag Bal. Its use of the dead and exploitation of souls threatens communities as well as the living world.'},
 {'fighters guild','The Fighters Guild is a cross-regional association of professional warriors. Its contracts can protect settlements and confront dangers beyond the capacity of local guards.'},
 {'mages guild','The Mages Guild promotes magical study and provides an institutional home for scholars across Tamriel. Its activities can connect local mysteries with wider magical dangers.'},
 {'dark brotherhood','The Dark Brotherhood is a secretive organization devoted to assassination and Sithis. Its contracts place personal loyalty and payment in tension with the lives of its targets.'},
 {'thieves guild','The Thieves Guild operates outside conventional law, relying on secrecy, contacts and illicit commerce. Helping it may build relationships in an underworld that ordinary authorities oppose.'},
 {'maulborn','The Maulborn are a source of unrest in Morrowind. Their activities threaten local communities and the authority of established Dunmer institutions.'},
 {'veiled heritance','The Veiled Heritance opposes Queen Ayrenn and her political direction. Its hostility to outsiders places the unity of the Aldmeri Dominion at risk.'},
 {'planemeld','The Planemeld is Molag Bal’s attempt to draw Nirn into Coldharbour. Resistance concerns the survival and freedom of the mortal world, not merely a local dispute.'},
 {'molag bal','Molag Bal is the Daedric Prince of domination and enslavement. His influence threatens mortal freedom, and Coldharbour is his realm of Oblivion.'},
 {'captain janeve','Janeve serves the Shornhelm Guard and is the younger sister of Countess Tamrith. Refugee protection in Rivenspire connects her military duties with the survival of civilians displaced by vampires.'},
 {'sir hughes','Sir Hughes is implicated in the killing of Duchess Lakana. The affair concerns accountability among the nobility and the security of the surrounding community.'},
 {'vivec','Vivec is one of the three living gods of the Dunmer Tribunal. His religious and political authority is central to Vvardenfell, where the Temple shapes public life.'},
 {'sotha sil','Sotha Sil is a member of the Tribunal and a master of magical engineering. His Clockwork City embodies an attempt to understand and reshape the laws of existence.'},
 {'almalexia','Almalexia is a living goddess of the Tribunal, revered in Morrowind as a protector. Her authority is bound to the religious and political institutions of the Dunmer.'},
 {'king emeric','Emeric leads the Daggerfall Covenant, a coalition of Bretons, Redguards and Orcs. Its unity depends on cooperation between peoples with distinct histories.'},
 {'jorunn','Jorunn the Skald-King leads the Ebonheart Pact, which brings together Nords, Dunmer and Argonians despite a history of conflict and enslavement.'},
 {'orcs','Orc communities often organize around strongholds and clan traditions. Their political position varies throughout Tamriel; Orsinium represents an important center of Orcish independence.'},
 {'ordinator','Ordinators serve the religious institutions of the Dunmer and enforce Temple authority. Their involvement often signals that a dispute has religious as well as civil significance.'},
 {'ashlander','Ashlanders maintain nomadic Dunmer traditions distinct from the settled Great Houses and Tribunal Temple. Their customs preserve older religious and ancestral practices.'},
 {'psijic order','The Psijic Order is an ancient magical tradition associated with Artaeum. Its members study powers and mysteries beyond conventional guild scholarship.'},
 {'undaunted','The Undaunted are adventurers who seek dangerous challenges and renown. Their expeditions bring outsiders into places that ordinary travelers might avoid.'},
 {'imperial legion','The Imperial Legion is a military institution of the Empire. During the Interregnum, competing claims to imperial authority complicate its role.'},
 {'reachmen','The Reachfolk are culturally distinct communities of the Reach, with their own spiritual traditions and clan identities. Their relationships with neighboring kingdoms have often been contested.'},
 {'gray host','The Gray Host is associated with vampires and werewolves and poses a threat to communities caught in its campaigns.'},
 {'house telvanni','House Telvanni is a Dunmer Great House known for independent wizard-lords and powerful magical traditions. Its hierarchy often values personal power and knowledge.'},
 {'house redoran','House Redoran is a Dunmer Great House whose traditions emphasize duty, martial prowess and honor.'},
 {'house hlaalu','House Hlaalu is a Dunmer Great House strongly associated with commerce and diplomacy. Its interests often intersect with trade and political negotiation.'},
 {'hist','The Hist are sentient trees central to Argonian spiritual and communal life. Their relationship with Argonians is especially important in Black Marsh.'},
 {'mara','Mara is a Divine associated with love, compassion and family. Her worship crosses many cultural boundaries.'},
 {'meridia','Meridia is a Daedric Prince associated with light and life energies and hostility to undeath. Opposition to necromancy does not necessarily imply respect for mortal autonomy.'},
 {'sheogorath','Sheogorath is the Daedric Prince of Madness. Encounters with his influence may challenge ordinary assumptions about reason and reality.'},
}

